<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/6th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Campaign</p><h1 class="enc-title">Göktürk–Sasanian destruction of the Hephthalites</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 557 CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gokturk-khaganate">Göktürk</a>–Sasanian destruction of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hephthalites">Hephthalites</a> was a joint campaign around 557 CE that ended the Hephthalite empire in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-asia">Central Asia</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sasanian-empire">Sasanian Empire</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khosrow-i">Khosrow I</a> expanded its control towards the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oxus">Amu Darya</a>, while the Göktürks took lands to the north.</p></div>
